WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.900
World Masterpiece Theater

00:07.800 --> 00:14.400
Homeless Child Remy

00:07.800 --> 00:14.400
"About Love"

00:15.260 --> 00:23.200
I continue wishing to see you

00:23.690 --> 00:28.360
Today we'll go on a journey

00:28.450 --> 00:32.310
That's as endless as the blue sky

00:32.820 --> 00:40.990
With joy, sorrow and hope come setbacks

00:41.360 --> 00:46.040
They repeat, they repeat

00:46.280 --> 00:50.870
What should I believe?

00:51.510 --> 00:59.880
You know nothing about love, however

01:00.320 --> 01:08.900
Someday you will feel warmth inside

01:09.730 --> 01:19.860
I dream of the day when you'll speak of love

01:20.860 --> 01:28.660
Tomorrow, our journey will begin

01:29.510 --> 01:35.020
Presented by:
Takara Fansubs & Migoto

01:35.000 --> 01:35.040
Achoo

01:35.040 --> 01:39.900
Episode 12:
The Snowy Mountain of Sadness

01:49.200 --> 01:51.530
Uhhh... So cold...

01:56.520 --> 01:58.500
Good morning. Cold, isn't it?

02:02.030 --> 02:03.750
You guys are lively.

02:05.480 --> 02:07.870
I wonder how far we're going today.

02:07.870 --> 02:09.510
Good morning.

02:09.890 --> 02:12.140
Did you have a good sleep last night?

02:12.140 --> 02:13.850
Yes, I did.

02:14.470 --> 02:16.720
It's cold this morning, isn't it?

02:16.720 --> 02:19.390
It's going to snow this afternoon.

02:19.390 --> 02:20.840
Snow?

02:22.140 --> 02:25.900
Look. The mountain's turned white.

02:26.540 --> 02:27.620
Yes.

02:31.250 --> 02:34.870
By the way, how is your boss?

02:34.870 --> 02:36.950
Mr. Vitalis? He's fine.

02:36.950 --> 02:39.160
That's good.

02:39.160 --> 02:42.980
When you guys came in last night asking for a place to stay,

02:42.980 --> 02:45.660
he looked very sick. That's why...

02:45.660 --> 02:46.470
Huh?

02:51.230 --> 02:53.220
Oh, yes.

02:53.550 --> 02:55.910
Before you leave, come inside and pick up some bread.

02:55.910 --> 02:57.720
I baked it myself.

02:57.720 --> 02:58.850
Thank you.

02:58.850 --> 03:01.070
No... It's my pleasure.

03:01.070 --> 03:04.270
We should help each other when we're in trouble.

03:11.890 --> 03:12.950
Mr. Vitalis.

03:13.860 --> 03:15.450
Early raiser.

03:15.450 --> 03:16.950
You're already up?

03:17.850 --> 03:19.640
Don't you feel ill?

03:19.640 --> 03:20.870
How do you feel?

03:20.870 --> 03:23.120
Feel ill?

03:26.260 --> 03:28.120
I'm fine.

03:28.120 --> 03:31.110
That's the only good trait about me, my body's strong.

03:31.110 --> 03:33.310
That's great.

03:36.170 --> 03:37.640
Ah?

03:37.640 --> 03:40.500
Joli-Coeur's still sleeping.

03:46.320 --> 03:48.320
You're sensitive to the cold.

03:48.320 --> 03:54.380
Joli-Coeur was born in a Southern warm country, so he's very frail to the cold.

03:54.380 --> 03:55.320
I see.

04:47.120 --> 04:48.750
Mr. Vitalis.

04:54.710 --> 04:58.150
It's no good. Seems like there'll be no gathering crowd.

04:58.670 --> 05:02.350
It's so cold. Nobody wants to stop on the street.

05:02.350 --> 05:03.940
That's true.

05:03.940 --> 05:06.520
Let's pack up for today and find an inn.

05:06.520 --> 05:07.900
But, what about the money?

05:08.340 --> 05:10.900
We can manage for tonight.

05:12.170 --> 05:12.880
Okay.

05:15.170 --> 05:15.950
Wait up!

05:20.700 --> 05:22.200
Wow... A monkey!

05:25.960 --> 05:28.450
Why is this monkey here?

05:33.000 --> 05:36.050
Hey, can that monkey do anything else?

05:36.430 --> 05:37.960
Of course.

05:37.960 --> 05:41.040
Joli-Coeur is a star of Vitalis' Troupe.

05:42.330 --> 05:43.960
And the rest of us, too.

05:45.380 --> 05:48.680
Wow... These dogs, too?

05:48.680 --> 05:50.440
Hey, show us something.

05:50.440 --> 05:52.240
All right.

05:52.240 --> 05:55.400
Guys, are you ready?

05:57.760 --> 05:58.900
Wow...

05:59.240 --> 06:01.070
Awesome! Awesome!

06:15.560 --> 06:18.670
<i>Good. Thanks to Joli-Coeur.</i>

06:43.500 --> 06:44.780
Joli-Coeur!

06:45.570 --> 06:47.170
Joli-Coeur.

06:48.570 --> 06:51.670
Joli-Coeur, hold on. Joli-Coeur.

07:00.800 --> 07:01.800
Snow?

07:19.940 --> 07:24.070
Joli-Coeur. Joli-Coeur, hold on.

08:07.880 --> 08:10.490
Mr. Vitalis. How's Joli-Coeur?

08:10.490 --> 08:11.660
Still the same.

08:12.910 --> 08:14.170
Joli-Coeur.

08:26.240 --> 08:27.810
What's wrong, Dolce?

08:54.090 --> 08:57.390
Mr. Vitalis. Is Joli-Coeur all right?

08:57.390 --> 09:01.340
He might have some broken bones. And he has a high temperature.

09:02.600 --> 09:03.800
Joli-Coeur.

09:04.420 --> 09:06.510
Joli-Coeur, hold on.

09:08.440 --> 09:09.800
Joli-Coeur.

09:15.370 --> 09:17.620
He's trying to perform.

09:26.820 --> 09:28.330
Pitiful.

09:29.230 --> 09:31.600
Mr. Vitalis, what should we do?

09:34.980 --> 09:38.580
In his condition, it's difficult for me to treat him.

09:39.430 --> 09:41.490
He cannot survive without a doctor.

09:55.170 --> 09:56.560
A veterinarian?

09:56.940 --> 10:00.060
We don't have one in this town.

10:00.060 --> 10:02.640
We don't even have a doctor for human beings.

10:02.640 --> 10:05.070
How far do we need to go to see a doctor?

10:05.070 --> 10:08.160
You could go to a town in the north...

10:08.900 --> 10:13.420
But even the nearest town is still very far from here.

10:13.420 --> 10:15.290
Remy, get our stuff prepared.

10:15.290 --> 10:16.000
Okay.

10:16.000 --> 10:17.830
Oh... Wait.

10:17.830 --> 10:20.790
It's no use. You can't go to that town.

10:20.790 --> 10:22.310
Why?

10:22.310 --> 10:26.050
Due to the storm the other day, the cliff collapsed.

10:26.050 --> 10:28.110
The path is blocked.

10:28.760 --> 10:30.610
Is there any other way?

10:30.760 --> 10:37.610
There's a path going over the mountain. But there's so much snow...

10:37.610 --> 10:39.270
A mountain path.

10:39.940 --> 10:44.270
You should know that going over the mountain in this season could be dangerous.

10:45.060 --> 10:47.610
If I were you, I wouldn't do something so risky.

10:49.550 --> 10:50.740
Mr. Vitalis.

10:51.280 --> 10:54.890
We need to hurry and send Joli-Coeur to a doctor, right?

10:57.800 --> 10:59.190
He looks like he's in pain.

10:59.190 --> 11:00.780
Let's hurry and go.

11:00.780 --> 11:02.290
But going over the mountain is...

11:02.830 --> 11:05.050
I will be all right. I can walk.

11:05.050 --> 11:07.450
I won't complain.

11:07.450 --> 11:09.300
Please, Mr.Vitalis.

11:14.630 --> 11:16.220
Mr. Vitalis.

11:16.590 --> 11:20.230
There's no other way to save Joli-Coeur, is there?

11:45.870 --> 11:48.320
We're heading northwards from here.

11:48.320 --> 11:49.960
Stay with me.

11:49.960 --> 11:51.530
Follow carefully.

11:52.100 --> 11:52.970
Okay.

12:15.830 --> 12:17.950
Remy, are you all right?

12:17.950 --> 12:19.750
Yes.

12:42.060 --> 12:43.230
Ah!

12:43.230 --> 12:44.310
Remy!?

12:46.690 --> 12:48.060
Remy!?

12:51.060 --> 12:52.740
Are you all right, Remy?

12:52.740 --> 12:53.950
Sorry.

12:54.890 --> 12:57.240
Remy, be careful.

12:57.240 --> 13:00.490
I can't let you get hurt.

13:01.970 --> 13:02.750
Okay.

13:06.080 --> 13:07.710
It's starting to snow again.

13:08.160 --> 13:09.510
Is it gonna be hard?

13:09.510 --> 13:10.710
Probably...

13:12.410 --> 13:14.220
Can we get over the mountain today?

13:15.700 --> 13:18.670
We have to, otherwise Joli-Coeur won't survive.

13:23.490 --> 13:24.770
Joli-Coeur.

13:27.340 --> 13:29.150
Let's go, Mr. Vitalis.

13:46.260 --> 13:47.750
Hang in there, Remy.

13:48.500 --> 13:49.410
Okay.

13:56.930 --> 13:58.260
Mr. Vitalis!

13:59.580 --> 14:01.010
Mr. Vitalis!

14:01.440 --> 14:03.320
Mr. Vitalis!

14:07.850 --> 14:08.900
What should I do?

14:11.010 --> 14:14.480
Capi? Zerbino! Dolce!

14:14.890 --> 14:16.760
Where are you guys!?

14:20.340 --> 14:21.990
Mr. Vitalis!

14:35.260 --> 14:36.640
Mr. Vitalis!

15:01.720 --> 15:02.660
Ah...

15:04.870 --> 15:07.340
Zerbino! Dolce!

15:08.260 --> 15:10.330
You came to find me.

15:13.570 --> 15:16.340
Take me to Mr. Vitalis.

15:16.690 --> 15:18.180
Remy!

15:18.900 --> 15:20.510
Where are you?

15:28.560 --> 15:29.510
I'm all right.

15:29.510 --> 15:31.220
Mr. Vitalis!

15:31.890 --> 15:33.650
Mr. Vitalis!

15:34.250 --> 15:35.970
Remy!

15:35.970 --> 15:36.900
Remy!

15:37.500 --> 15:40.180
I'm here! Right here!

15:42.700 --> 15:44.340
Mr. Vitalis!

15:44.340 --> 15:45.200
Remy!

15:51.100 --> 15:52.370
Good.

15:53.790 --> 15:56.050
Are you hurt?

15:56.050 --> 15:56.920
No.

15:57.510 --> 15:59.070
Just a little further.

15:59.070 --> 16:00.630
We must have just passed through the rough spot.

16:01.050 --> 16:02.490
Good.

16:08.400 --> 16:12.150
Let's find a place to have a rest and take shelter from the storm.

16:12.150 --> 16:13.240
Okay.

16:26.450 --> 16:28.830
Joli-Coeur, how do you feel?

16:31.040 --> 16:33.950
We're almost there. Hold on.

16:33.950 --> 16:37.300
We'll get you to the doctor soon.

16:40.960 --> 16:43.230
Well, let's get started.

16:43.230 --> 16:44.260
Okay.

16:50.420 --> 16:52.680
What's wrong with you, guys?

16:55.320 --> 16:56.310
Mr. Vitalis.

16:58.510 --> 16:59.570
Wolves.

17:00.190 --> 17:01.270
Wolves?

17:29.490 --> 17:32.010
Remy, take care of Joli-Coeur.

17:32.010 --> 17:33.140
Right.

18:26.170 --> 18:27.500
Remy, run!

18:27.500 --> 18:28.490
But...

18:28.490 --> 18:29.710
Go! Now!

18:48.090 --> 18:49.640
Dolce!

18:53.830 --> 18:55.350
No, Zerbino!

18:55.350 --> 18:56.180
Remy.

19:04.400 --> 19:06.000
Zerbino...

19:06.000 --> 19:06.780
Zerbino!

19:21.570 --> 19:22.770
Mr. Vitalis.

19:34.730 --> 19:36.470
Go away!

19:36.990 --> 19:39.870
Please! Go away!

19:39.870 --> 19:40.480
Capi!

19:46.750 --> 19:47.440
Remy...

20:01.200 --> 20:02.430
Mr. Vitalis.

20:02.430 --> 20:04.870
You did well, Remy.

20:04.870 --> 20:06.560
Remy, everything's all right now.

20:09.130 --> 20:11.130
Dolce, Zerbino?

20:15.080 --> 20:16.180
No...

20:29.410 --> 20:31.520
Dolce... Zerbino...

20:37.780 --> 20:38.870
No.

20:38.870 --> 20:40.620
I can't believe it!

20:45.180 --> 20:46.520
Ohow...

20:46.520 --> 20:47.760
Mr. Vitalis.

20:47.760 --> 20:49.890
It's nothing serious.

20:49.890 --> 20:51.090
I'm all right.

20:51.090 --> 20:52.510
Take care of Joli-Coeur.

20:54.500 --> 20:55.870
He's cold.

20:55.870 --> 20:57.280
Very cold.

20:57.280 --> 20:58.260
Joli-Coeur is...

20:58.870 --> 21:01.810
No... He's still breathing slightly.

21:01.810 --> 21:02.700
Oww...

21:04.230 --> 21:05.330
Now, let's go.

21:05.330 --> 21:08.770
No, it's too late. He won't survive.

21:09.240 --> 21:11.060
Yes, he will survive.

21:11.060 --> 21:13.910
We can't waste Dolce and Zerbino's death.

21:13.910 --> 21:16.290
We must save Joli-Coeur.

21:21.490 --> 21:23.910
Keep moving forward, Remy.

21:25.550 --> 21:27.190
Dolce.

21:27.190 --> 21:28.130
Zerbino.

21:35.530 --> 21:36.760
I'm sorry...

21:37.540 --> 21:38.760
I'm sorry...

21:39.550 --> 21:47.730
Try to love yourself more

21:44.150 --> 21:46.540
<i>Joli-Coeur will survive,</i>

21:46.540 --> 21:47.600
<i>he will survive.</i>

21:48.250 --> 21:50.060
<i>I won't let him die.</i>

21:49.300 --> 21:58.550
Abandoned dreams can be seen again

21:58.840 --> 22:07.280
Surely, not everyone can be so strong

22:08.500 --> 22:19.410
The blue sky lifts all of the world's tears...

22:19.910 --> 22:29.540
Tomorrow's courage comes

22:29.810 --> 22:39.550
From the future that gives us our fate

22:39.730 --> 22:48.460
Try to seek for them more

22:49.360 --> 22:53.060
Give your heart to

22:53.260 --> 23:08.470
That person who is also seeking you

23:20.620 --> 23:21.870
Joli-Coeur will survive.

23:24.010 --> 23:27.190
Remy, go to Paris by yourself.

23:27.190 --> 23:28.620
No, No!

23:29.560 --> 23:33.170
I will survive in your heart.

23:33.170 --> 23:36.550
<i>Farewell on a Snowy Day</i>

23:33.170 --> 23:36.550
Next time:
